{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"chatcmpl-54aaf929-4e20-42c2-8179-7313dd9b8a15","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"chatcmpl-tool-b6bd41399c17974a","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/private/var/folders/h5/l8qslbp55w5621qf9ngsh5jc0000gn/T/epic-RHAISTRAT-9013-6ke_9be1/artifacts/epic-tasks/RHAISTRAT-9013-E001.md","content":"# FIPS 140-3 crypto remediation for KServe serving images\n\n## Description\n\nMake every KServe component image (control plane and data plane) run correctly on\nFIPS-enabled OpenShift clusters using validated cryptographic modules, with no\nnon-validated crypto in the request path. This epic also delivers the KServe\nportion of the FIPS regression enforcement and the inputs to the compliance\nevidence package.\n\n## Scope\n\n- Audit all KServe images for non-validated cryptographic library usage and\n  produce a per-image module inventory (libraries, versions, linkage, validation\n  status).\n- Remediate each flagged image to link only validated crypto modules (library\n  swaps, rebuilds, base-image changes as needed) without changing functional\n  behavior.\n- Verify the remediated images on FIPS-enabled OpenShift clusters in both\n  supported deployment modes (serverless and raw deployment).\n- Author and verify the portion of the CI FIPS regression gating check that\n  covers KServe builds: a gating check that fails any KServe build reintroducing\n  non-validated crypto usage.\n- Build the remediated images through the existing build pipeline (KServe is\n  already onboarded) so that signed build attestations are produced and\n  retrievable for the compliance evidence package.\n- Hand off the module inventory, build attestations, and FIPS test results for\n  aggregation into the compliance evidence package.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- A module inventory exists for every KServe image, enumerating each crypto\n  library, its version, and its validation status.\n- Scanning the built KServe images confirms no non-validated crypto modules are\n  linked in the request path.\n- Remediated images pass functional verification on a FIPS-enabled OpenShift\n  cluster in both serverless and raw deployment modes.\n- The CI FIPS regression check gates KServe builds and is verified to fail a\n  deliberately non-compliant test build that reintroduces non-validated crypto\n  usage.\n- Remediated images build green in the existing build pipeline and their signed\n  attestations are retrievable for the evidence package.\n\n## HLR Traceability\n\n- **HLR-1 (P0)** — KServe serving images run on FIPS-enabled clusters using\n  validated crypto modules.\n- **HLR-3 (P1)** — authors and verifies the CI FIPS regression gating check\n  covering KServe builds. Bundled with the P0 remediation: the check shares the\n  build surfaces, image inventories, and scan tooling of the remediation it\n  enforces, so it is not separately schedulable — a standalone enforcement epic\n  would re-audit the same builds.\n\n## Risks / Notes\n\n- The audit determines which specific images and libraries need work, but not\n  the approach (audit → remediate → verify → enforce); the epic proceeds the\n  same way regardless of the audit outcome.\n"}}],"model":"rits/zai-org/glm-5-3","stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":44909,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-8bd6d5ec5bce34b1","agent_id":"a1c09ab8cd02268e5","session_id":"b908e981-68fd-4e98-a28a-ee0224758c04","uuid":"cf089754-70fb-4f98-9db0-e660f7686710","timestamp":"2026-10-26T20:23:44.247Z","subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Decompose RHAISTRAT-9013 into epics"}
