odules are linked\n  in the request path.\n- The remediated image passes functional verification on a FIPS-enabled\n  OpenShift cluster, including install/upgrade and reconciliation of managed\n  serving components.\n- The CI FIPS regression check gates Platform Operator builds and is verified to\n  fail a deliberately non-compliant test build that reintroduces non-validated\n  crypto usage.\n- The remediated image builds green in the existing build pipeline and its\n  signed attestations are retrievable for the evidence package.\n\n## HLR Traceability\n\n- **HLR-1 (P0)** — the Platform Operator image runs on FIPS-enabled clusters\n  using validated crypto modules.\n- **HLR-3 (P1)** — authors and verifies the CI FIPS regression gating check\n  covering Platform Operator builds. Bundled with the P0 remediation: the check\n  shares the build surfaces and scan tooling of the remediation it enforces, so\n  it is not separately schedulable — a standalone enforcement epic would\n  re-audit the same builds.\n\n## Risks / Notes\n\n- No architecture-context file exists for the Platform Operator, so its target\n  repo, surfaces, and owning team are unverified; confirm the repo and owner\n  before scheduling.\n- The audit determines which specific libraries need work, but not the approach\n  (audit → remediate → verify → enforce); the epic proceeds the same way\n  regardless of the audit outcome.\n"}}],"model":"rits/zai-org/glm-5-3","stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":44909,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-8bd6d5ec5bce34b1","agent_id":"a1c09ab8cd02268e5","session_id":"b908e981-68fd-4e98-a28a-ee0224758c04","uuid":"327fb063-4a69-4b4e-9158-027cbf582303","timestamp":"2026-10-26T20:23:51.092Z","subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Decompose RHAISTRAT-9013 into epics"}
