{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-a52b071694f34961","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-9013\n3\tepic_count: 4\n4\tcritical_path_length: 3\n5\tdecompose_complete: true\n6\trevised: false\n7\ttriage: null\n8\ttriage_rationale: null\n9\t---\n10\t# Decomposition Summary — RHAISTRAT-9013 (FIPS 140-3 compliance for the model serving stack)\n11\t\n12\tStrategy status: Refinement Done. Strategy priority: Critical. Affected components:\n13\tKServe, Platform Operator.\n14\t\n15\t## Epic List\n16\t\n17\t| ID | Title | Type | Team | Priority |\n18\t|----|-------|------|------|----------|\n19\t| RHAISTRAT-9013-E001 | FIPS 140-3 crypto remediation for KServe serving images | Implementation | RHOAI Serving | P0 |\n20\t| RHAISTRAT-9013-E002 | FIPS 140-3 crypto remediation for the Platform Operator image | Implementation | RHOAI Platform | P0 |\n21\t| RHAISTRAT-9013-E003 | FIPS 140-3 compliance evidence package and certification submission | Implementation | RHOAI Serving | P0 |\n22\t| RHAISTRAT-9013-E004 | FIPS support posture documentation | Implementation (docs-authoring) | RHOAI Documentation | P0 |\n23\t\n24\tNotes on assignments:\n25\t- E001 team and repo surface come from the KServe architecture context file\n26\t  (`.context/architecture-context/architecture/rhoai-3.0/kserve.md`: owning team\n27\t  RHOAI Serving, midstream `opendatahub-io/kserve`, Konflux-onboarded).\n28\t- E003 spans both affected components (it aggregates evidence from the KServe and\n29\t  Platform Operator remediation work); it is assigned the single most-relevant\n30\t  canonical component, KServe, because the strategy targets the model serving\n31\t  stack of which KServe is the primary component.\n32\t- E004 is assigned the canonical `Documentation` component (Red Hat docs content\n33\t  process → `docs-authoring`).\n34\t- Team assignments for E002 and E004 are inferred — the strategy has no Impacted\n35\t  Teams table (see Health Warnings).\n36\t\n37\t## Dependency DAG\n38\t\n39\t```mermaid\n40\tgraph TD\n41\t    E001[RHAISTRAT-9013-E001 KServe remediation] --> E003[RHAISTRAT-9013-E003 evidence package]\n42\t    E002[RHAISTRAT-9013-E002 Platform Operator remediation] --> E003\n43\t    E001 --> E004[RHAISTRAT-9013-E004 docs]\n44\t    E002 --> E004\n45\t    E003 --> E004\n46\t```\n47\t\n48\t## DAG Justification\n49\t\n50\t| Edge | Rule | Rationale |\n51\t|------|------|-----------|\n52\t| E001 → E003 | Rule 12/13 (artifact producer → consumer) | The evidence package documents the remediated KServe images, their module inventory, and FIPS test results; it cannot be assembled before that work exists. Build attestations, however, are consumed as content: expressed as an acceptance criterion on E003, never as an edge to any build-pipeline work. |\n53\t| E002 → E003 | Rule 12/13 (artifact producer → consumer) | Same: evidence for the Platform Operator image depends on its remediation results. |\n54\t| E001 → E004 | Rule 11 (docs last) | docs-authoring epic blocked by every Implementation epic in the strategy. |\n55\t| E002 → E004 | Rule 11 (docs last) | Same. |\n56\t| E003 → E004 | Rule 11 (docs last) | Same. |\n57\t| (no edge) E001 ∥ E002 | Rule 14 (different components/repos) | Remediation work in different components with no shared artifacts runs in parallel. |\n58\t| (no edge) build pipelines → E003 | Rule 13 / Rule 10 | KServe is already Konflux-onboarded per architecture context, so no onboarding epics are generated; the signed attestations the evidence package needs are a configuration/content reference — an AC on E003, not a DAG dependency. |\n59\t| (no epic) CI FIPS regression gate | Shared-surface enforcement rule | HLR-3's gating check spans the exact builds and images the remediation epics modify — it is divided per surface into E001 and E002 (each authors and verifies the portion covering its own builds), not carved into a standalone work-type epic. |\n60\t\n61\t## HLR Traceability Matrix\n62\t\n63\t| HLR | Priority | Epic(s) | Coverage |\n64\t|-----|----------|---------|----------|\n65\t| HLR-1 | P0 | E001, E002 | E001 covers all KServe images; E002 covers the Platform Operator image. Together they cover \"all serving-stack images\" across the strategy's affected components. |\n66\t| HLR-2 | P0 | E003 | Evidence package (module inventory, build attestations, test results) assembled and submitted through the security review board to the external certification lab. |\n67\t| HLR-3 | P1 | E001, E002 (bundled) — the CI gating check shares the build surfaces, image inventories, and scan tooling of the P0 remediation it enforces; per the shared-surface enforcement rule it is divided per surface into the epic that owns each surface, and a standalone CI epic would re-audit the same builds twice. Not separately schedulable. | Each remediation epic authors and verifies the portion of the FIPS regression gating check covering its own component's builds. |\n68\t| HLR-4 | P2 | E004 | Documentation of FIPS support posture and cluster prerequisites; docs-authoring priority derived from strategy priority Critical → P0 per the docs-authoring priority exception. |\n69\t\n70\tAll four HLRs are covered; none orphaned.\n71\t\n72\t## Health Warnings\n73\t\n74\t1. **Missing strategy sections.** The strategy has no Impacted Teams table, no\n75\t   Dependencies table, no Acceptance Criteria (Given/When/Then) section, and no\n76\t   Non-Functional Requirements; the Affected Components section is a bare list\n77\t   without per-component change descriptions or owner teams. Decomposition\n78\t   proceeded from the HLRs and the component list; team assignments for E002\n79\t   (Platform Operator) and E004 (Documentation) are inferred and need human\n80\t   verification.\n81\t2. **Platform Operator has no architecture-context file.**\n82\t   `.context/architecture-context/` contains only `kserve.md`. The Platform\n83\t   Operator's repos, surfaces, and owning team could not be corroborated. It is\n84\t   treated as an existing component being remediated — it appears in the canonical\n85\t   RHAI component list (`.context/rhai-components.txt`) and the strategy presumes\n86\t   it exists (\"affected component\"), so no onboarding chain was generated — but\n87\t   this premise is unverified; flag for human review. AI signal\n88\t   `architecture_claims` is scored 0 for E002.\n89\t3. **Scope ambiguity — \"serving data plane\".** The problem statement says \"KServe\n90\t   components and the serving data plane link non-validated crypto libraries\",\n91\t   but Affected Components lists only KServe and Platform Operator. Per the KServe\n92\t   architecture context, the serving data plane executes on Serving Runtimes\n93\t   (vLLM, OpenVINO, Caikit), which are NOT listed as affected, and the\n94\t   out-of-scope list does not mention them. If the data-plane runtime images are\n95\t   in scope, an additional Serving Runtimes remediation epic is required. The\n96\t   decomposition follows the Affected Components list (the authoritative input to\n97\t   epic generation); human verification needed before execution.\n98\t4. **External schedule gates are risks, not acceptance criteria.** Certification\n99\t   lab turnaround (historically six to nine months) and security review board\n100\t   cadence are externally controlled and cannot be compressed by engineering\n101\t   effort. They are recorded as Risks/Notes on the evidence epic; the AC sits at\n102\t   the engineering completion point we control (package assembled and submitted).\n103\t5. **Priority notes (not inversions).** HLR-3 (P1) is bundled into the P0\n104\t   remediation epics (see traceability row for rationale), and HLR-4 (P2) maps to\n105\t   a P0 docs epic because the docs-authoring priority exception derives it from\n106\t   the strategy's Critical priority. Both are rule-driven.\n107\t\n108\t## Tiered Delivery\n109\t\n110\tThe external certification dependency has uncertain timing, and the strategy can\n111\tdeliver partial value without it:\n112\t\n113\t- **Tier 1 (independent value):** E001 and E002. FIPS-capable serving-stack\n114\t  images plus CI regression enforcement deliver user-facing value (the serving\n115\t  stack runs correctly on FIPS-enabled OpenShift clusters) without certification.\n116\t- **Tier 2 (dependency-gated):** E003 (evidence package and submission — gated on\n117\t  the Tier 1 remediation results and, externally, on review-board and lab\n118\t  timing) and E004 (blocked by all Implementation epics per the docs-last rule).\n119\t\n120\t## Component Mapping Notes\n121\t\n122\t- All epic `component` values are verbatim from `.context/rhai-components.txt`:\n123\t  `KServe` (E001, E003), `Platform Operator` (E002), `Documentation` (E004).\n124\t- E003 spans KServe and Platform Operator; assigned `KServe` as the single most\n125\t  relevant canonical name (noted above).\n126\t\n127\t## Investigation Epic Decision\n128\t\n129\tNo Investigation epics were generated. The strategy declares \"None on scope\" for\n130\topen questions; the remaining unknown — exactly which images link which\n131\tnon-validated crypto libraries — does not change which epics exist (both affected\n132\tcomponents are declared affected regardless) or their approach (audit →\n133\tremediate → verify → enforce). Per the unclear-passage distinction this is an\n134\timplementation detail resolved when each remediation epic starts, captured as the\n135\tmodule-inventory acceptance criterion on E001 and E002. Lab scheduling and\n136\treview-board cadence are external schedule constraints (Health Warning 4), not\n137\ttechnical unknowns.\n138\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-948e3da349f9a6f4","agent_id":"a1e7e1f7b68137c2b","session_id":"b908e981-68fd-4e98-a28a-ee0224758c04","uuid":"0847d414-f408-4ea2-a724-bfe432875f18","timestamp":"2026-10-26T20:25:08.464Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-a52b071694f34961","permission_decision":